{"uid":"7fd729612d4438ed","name":"test_none_of_the_four_witnesses_still_increments_the_counter","fullName":"tests.test_worker_hat#test_none_of_the_four_witnesses_still_increments_the_counter","historyId":"abf418e17c82094e9b96d10a0a9099b4","time":{"start":1791866914651,"stop":1791866914771,"duration":120},"description":"The guard this must NOT weaken: three ordinary no-op iterations\n    (no tasks.json change, no commit, no contract payload, no tool-call\n    evidence) still trip the counter exactly as before this task, even\n    with a real git workspace present and simply never touched. This\n    drives `_step_worker()` directly (default `max_approaches=1`, i.e.\n    the LAST approach) rather than the full `_run_job_core()` dispatch\n    loop, because on the LAST approach task 012 (requirement B.3) changes\n    what happens once the counter fires: the run now pauses and\n    escalates (`tests/test_last_approach.py` is\n    that pause's own dedicated coverage) instead of ending `failed` on\n    paperwork, and a run parked on that pause inside `_run_job_core()`\n    would sit forever awaiting a `resume()` this test never sends. The\n    counter itself is unchanged either way -- the log line still fires.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The guard this must NOT weaken: three ordinary no-op iterations<br />\n(no tasks.json change, no commit, no contract payload, no tool-call<br />\nevidence) still trip the counter exactly as before this task, even<br />\nwith a real git workspace present and simply never touched. This<br />\ndrives <code>_step_worker()</code> directly (default <code>max_approaches=1</code>, i.e.<br />\nthe LAST approach) rather than the full <code>_run_job_core()</code> dispatch<br />\nloop, because on the LAST approach task 012 (requirement B.3) changes<br />\nwhat happens once the counter fires: the run now pauses and<br />\nescalates (<code>tests/test_last_approach.py</code> is<br />\nthat pause's own dedicated coverage) instead of ending <code>failed</c